<title>POLAND: Polish 1996 yr/yr CPI 18.5 pct vs 21.6 pct in 1995.</title>
<headline>Polish 1996 yr/yr CPI 18.5 pct vs 21.6 pct in 1995.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish consumer prices rose 1.3 percent in December against a 1.3 percent rise in November, bringing year-on-year inflation down to 18.5 percent, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>The index rose 18.5 percent in all of 1996 compared with a 21.6 percent rise in 1995.  </p>
<p> POLISH CONSUMER PRICES    DECEMBER 96   NOV 96    DEC 95</p>
<p> month/month change (pct)     1.3	   1.3	  1.5</p>
<p> yr/yr change		    18.5	  19.1	 21.6</p>
<p> services m/m change	    0.3	   0.6	  0.6</p>
<p> services yr/yr change	 19.5	  19.8	 21.9</p>
<p> food prices m/m change	 2.4	   2.2	  1.9</p>
<p> food prices yr/yr change    19.0	  19.3	 18.8</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
